      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:2jmzz7'
    '|a||So a manager with slack can swap the owners'' profit for size.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Raise the floor to the owners'' best, eight hundred and twenty-five thousand, and her slack is gone: thirty-five boats.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||But Herbert Simon doubted anyone maximises at all. Firms take the first plan that clears the bar and stop looking. He called it satisficing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1v7y9e5'
    '|a||On this picture, anything from twenty-five to forty-five boats is good enough. The peak is just one of many.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1uyi8vi'
    '|a||Here''s my reply. A boatyard run below its best is a bargain: a raider can buy the shares, sack the manager, and pocket the difference.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:51bz1t'
    '|a||That''s what Henry Manne called the market for corporate control, in 1965. The real floor is set by the next bidder, not by sleepy owners.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1vb4q5g'
    '|b||Then take the bidder away and watch. In the 1980s, many US states passed laws that made hostile takeovers harder.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:18jtzvj'
    '|b||Marianne Bertrand and Sendhil Mullainathan compared firms the laws shielded with firms they didn''t.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:ng1fvu'
    '|a||In the shielded firms, white-collar pay rose about four percent.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:191v9wk'
    '|a||Fewer old plants closed, fewer new ones opened, and productivity and profits fell.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1a82653'
    '|b||So not an empire. A quiet life. Your bidder matters, but unwatched managers drift toward comfort, not size.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1xpcri5'
    '|a||I''ll take that. Managers drift when nobody can strike: mostly agreed. Toward size or toward comfort: contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ua3hem'
    '|b||Want the boatyard''s numbers worked out? Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:mwo9af'
    '|a||Revenue is Q times a price of a hundred minus Q, cost is four hundred plus thirty a boat, so profit is seventy Q minus Q squared minus four hundred.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12640
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||It tops out where its slope, seventy minus two Q, is zero: thirty-five boats.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:uo1qb3'
    '|b||Set profit equal to the floor of seven hundred and twenty-five: two roots, twenty-five and forty-five, and the sales maximiser takes the larger.':
